# WT-3-prod-multidevice — Linux laptop device template.
#
# This device runs the driver (:18092) and hosts the codex CLI with
# `.codex/config.toml` on prod runbook path (a) local proxy
# (http://127.0.0.1:53452/v1).
#
# HARNESS-ONLY: this file is a template. Real OAuth tokens are NEVER
# committed — the oauth_placeholder value below MUST stay literally
# `<OAUTH_TOKEN_HERE_DO_NOT_COMMIT>`. Real tokens live outside the
# repo (in the operator's `~/.codex/tokens.yaml`) and are gitignored
# via the multi-agent/.gitignore rules that re-ignore any tokens.yaml
# / *.token / *.pem under this directory.
#
# Real-device usage: paper/v3/p3-prod-multidevice-run.

kind: device
role: driver
device_kind: laptop
listen: 127.0.0.1:18092
oauth_placeholder: <OAUTH_TOKEN_HERE_DO_NOT_COMMIT>
notes: |
  Driver device. Codex config lives in ~/.codex/config.toml (path (a)
  local proxy). Model provider block:
    [model_providers.modelserver]
    base_url = "http://127.0.0.1:53452/v1"
    experimental_bearer_token = "<OAUTH_TOKEN_HERE_DO_NOT_COMMIT>"
  Real bearer token comes from `codex auth login` on this device;
  never write it here.
